-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 6: ss 65 to 66, the liability of principals,
-- contractors and subcontractors for the salary of a workman, and the registration of contractors.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)" marks the branches that rest on
-- one of the two readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).
--
-- PERIODS OF DAYS.  Sections 65(2A) and 66(4) count days after an event.  They are read as a
-- period of days from the event, which the Interpretation Act 1965 s 50 counts (staged in
-- DEPENDENCIES as sgia-interpretation-time); the public holidays are a list the caller gives.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 6 Contractors and contracting, ss 65 to 66`

§§ `s 65 Liability of principals, contractors and subcontractors for salary of workman`

-- Seam S13: the answer asked for by s 116(3) (ea3), "liable as a principal under section 65 to pay
-- any salary due".  Subsection (1B) takes the principal out where the work is constructional and the
-- principal is not also a constructional contractor.
-- src:2481 | 65.—(1) Where a principal, in the course of or for the purposes of
-- src:2482 | or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal’s
-- src:2483 | trade or business, contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour
-- src:2484 | or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any
-- src:2485 | part of any work undertaken by the principal, and any salary is due to
-- src:2486 | any workman by the contractor or any subcontractor under the
-- src:2487 | contractor for labour supplied or for work done in the course of the
-- src:2488 | execution of such work, the principal and the contractor and any such
-- src:2489 | subcontractor (not being the employer) are jointly and severally liable
-- src:2490 | with the employer to pay the workman as if the workman had been
-- src:2491 | immediately employed by the principal, and where salary is claimed
-- src:2492 | from the principal, this Act (with the exception of section 33 relating
-- src:2497 | to priority of salary) applies as if reference to the principal were
-- src:2498 | substituted for reference to the employer, except that salary claimed is
-- src:2499 | to be calculated with reference to the salary of the workman under the
-- src:2500 | employer by whom the workman is immediately employed.
@ref s 65(1) (src:2481-2500)
GIVEN `the principal, in the course of or for the purposes of or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal's trade or business, contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `salary is due to a workman by the contractor or a subcontractor under the contractor for labour supplied or for work done in the course of the execution of such work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for constructional work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal is also a constructional contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a principal, in the course of or for the purposes of or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal’s trade or business, contracts with a contractor ... and any salary is due to any workman by the contractor or any subcontractor under the contractor" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "Where" not met
        IF NOT (`the principal, in the course of or for the purposes of or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal's trade or business, contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal` AND `salary is due to a workman by the contractor or a subcontractor under the contractor for labour supplied or for work done in the course of the execution of such work`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a contract for constructional work, the principal is not liable for the payment of salary under subsection (1) unless the principal is also a constructional contractor" -- marginal (a)
        IF `the contract is for constructional work` AND (NOT `the principal is also a constructional contractor`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 65(1) (src:2481-2500)
GIVEN `the principal, in the course of or for the purposes of or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal's trade or business, contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `salary is due to a workman by the contractor or a subcontractor under the contractor for labour supplied or for work done in the course of the execution of such work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(1) the contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is jointly and severally liable with the employer to pay the workman` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a principal, in the course of or for the purposes of or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal’s trade or business, contracts with a contractor ... and any salary is due to any workman by the contractor or any subcontractor under the contractor" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "Where" not met
        IF NOT (`the principal, in the course of or for the purposes of or in pursuance of or in furtherance of the interests of the principal's trade or business, contracts with a contractor for the supply of labour or for the execution by or under the contractor of the whole or any part of any work undertaken by the principal` AND `salary is due to a workman by the contractor or a subcontractor under the contractor for labour supplied or for work done in the course of the execution of such work`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the principal and the contractor and any such subcontractor (not being the employer) are jointly and severally liable with the employer" -- the person is the employer (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF `the person is the employer` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Where salary is claimed from the principal it "is to be calculated with reference to the salary of
-- the workman under the employer by whom the workman is immediately employed".
@ref s 65(1) (src:2481-2500)
GIVEN `the salary of the workman under the employer by whom the workman is immediately employed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 65(1) the salary claimed from the principal` MEANS
    `the salary of the workman under the employer by whom the workman is immediately employed`

-- The same sentence takes section 33, the priority of salary, out of the Act that applies to a claim on the principal.
-- It is the Act's own exception ("with the exception of"), so a claim on the principal gets a flat no.
-- A salary not claimed from the principal is outside the exception: the sentence is silent about it.
@ref s 65(1) (src:2481-2500)
GIVEN `the salary is claimed from the principal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(1) section 33 relating to priority of salary applies to the salary claimed from the principal` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where salary is claimed from the principal, this Act (with the exception of section 33 relating ... to priority of salary) applies"
    IF `the salary is claimed from the principal` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the exception speaks only of salary claimed from the principal
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2502 | (1A) No principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the
-- src:2503 | employer, is jointly and severally liable to any workman under
-- src:2504 | subsection (1) for more than the salary earned in one month for work
-- src:2505 | done by the employer.
@ref s 65(1A) (src:2502-2505)
GIVEN `the person is the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the salary due` IS A NUMBER
      `the salary earned in one month for work done by the employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 65(1A) the most a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, is liable for` MEANS
    IF `the person is the employer`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer"
    THEN NOTHING
    -- the cap, in the Act's words: "for more than the salary earned in one month for work done by the employer"
    ELSE JUST (min `the salary due` `the salary earned in one month for work done by the employer`)

-- src:2513 | (2) A workman who wishes to recover any salary from a person
-- src:2514 | liable under this section for the salary must, before lodging a claim for
-- src:2515 | the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016,
-- src:2516 | submit to the Commissioner, under section 3(1) of that Act, a
-- src:2517 | mediation request for the mediation under Part 2 of that Act of every
-- src:2518 | dispute for which the claim will be lodged.
@ref s 65(2) (src:2513-2518)
GIVEN `the workman wishes to recover salary from a person liable under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the workman has submitted to the Commissioner, under section 3(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016, a mediation request for the mediation under Part 2 of that Act of every dispute for which the claim will be lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2) the workman may lodge the claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A workman who wishes to recover any salary from a person liable under this section for the salary"
        IF NOT `the workman wishes to recover salary from a person liable under this section` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before lodging a claim for the salary under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016, submit to the Commissioner" a mediation request -- marginal (a)
        IF NOT `the workman has submitted to the Commissioner, under section 3(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016, a mediation request for the mediation under Part 2 of that Act of every dispute for which the claim will be lodged` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) makes the mediation request a condition and does not itself give the right to lodge the claim, which is the Employment Claims Act 2016's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The 60 days: counted from the day the salary becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3,
-- as a period of days from that event.  The Commissioner may extend the period (subsection (2B)).
-- src:2522 | (2A) The workman must submit the mediation request to the
-- src:2523 | Commissioner within 60 days after the date on which the salary
-- src:2524 | becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3.
@ref s 65(2A) (src:2522-2524)
GIVEN `the day the salary becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the day the salary becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3` 60 `the public holidays` FALSE

-- src:2528 | (2B) The Commissioner may extend the period under
-- src:2529 | subsection (2A) within which the workman must submit the
-- src:2530 | mediation request to the Commissioner.
@ref s 65(2B) (src:2528-2530)
GIVEN `the last day under subsection (2A)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day to which the Commissioner has extended the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day to which the Commissioner has extended the period`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Commissioner "may extend the period", and the subsection says nothing of how long
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day under subsection (2A)`
    WHEN JUST extended THEN
        CONSIDER `the last day under subsection (2A)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST original THEN JUST (IF extended GREATER THAN original THEN extended ELSE original)

-- src:2522 | (2A) The workman must submit the mediation request to the
-- src:2523 | Commissioner within 60 days after the date on which the salary
-- src:2524 | becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3.
@ref s 65(2A) (src:2522-2524)
GIVEN `the day the salary becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3` IS A DATE
      `the day the workman submitted the mediation request to the Commissioner` IS A DATE
      `the last day to which the Commissioner has extended the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2A) the mediation request was submitted within 60 days after the date on which the salary becomes due for payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 65(2B) the last day for submitting the mediation request as extended` (`s 65(2A) the last day for submitting the mediation request` `the day the salary becomes due for payment in accordance with Part 3` `the public holidays`) `the last day to which the Commissioner has extended the period`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the count of days comes from the Interpretation Act module, which gives no answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the day the workman submitted the mediation request to the Commissioner` AT MOST last)

DECLARE `s 65(2A) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 65(2A) the workman`

DECLARE `s 65(2A) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 65(2A) submit the mediation request to the Commissioner`

@ref s 65(2A) (src:2522-2524)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day the salary becomes due for payment to the last day for submitting the mediation request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 65(2A) Actor` `s 65(2A) Action`
`s 65(2A) the workman's duty to submit the mediation request` MEANS
    PARTY `s 65(2A) the workman`
    MUST `s 65(2A) submit the mediation request to the Commissioner`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day the salary becomes due for payment to the last day for submitting the mediation request`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 65(2A) the workman` BECAUSE "the workman did not submit the mediation request to the Commissioner within 60 days after the date on which the salary becomes due for payment"

-- Subsection (2C) is a dated shape: a claim lodged before 1 April 2017 under section 119.
-- src:2534 | (2C) However, if a workman has lodged, before 1 April 2017, a
-- src:2535 | claim under section 119 for any salary against a person liable under
-- src:2536 | this section for the salary —
-- src:2538 | (a) subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) do not apply to the recovery
-- src:2539 | of the salary under that claim; and
-- src:2541 | (b) instead, the repealed section 65(1C) and (2) as in force
-- src:2542 | immediately before 1 April 2017 continues to apply to the
-- src:2543 | recovery of the salary under that claim.
@ref s 65(2C) (src:2534-2543)
GIVEN `the workman lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claim was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2C)(a) subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` MEANS
    IF `the workman lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under this section` AND (`the day the claim was lodged` LESS THAN Date 1 4 2017)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsections (2), (2A) and (2B) do not apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a workman has lodged, before 1 April 2017, a claim under section 119 for any salary against a person liable under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 65(2C)(b) (src:2541-2543)
GIVEN `the workman lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claim was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2C)(b) the repealed section 65(1C) and (2) as in force immediately before 1 April 2017 continue to apply to the recovery of the salary under that claim` MEANS
    IF `the workman lodged a claim under section 119 for salary against a person liable under this section` AND (`the day the claim was lodged` LESS THAN Date 1 4 2017)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a workman has lodged, before 1 April 2017, a claim under section 119 for any salary against a person liable under this section" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a) and (b): an unmet "if", and a claim lodged on or after 1 April 2017 is outside the period the text fixes
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2550 | (3) Nothing in this section prevents any principal or contractor or
-- src:2551 | subcontractor, not being the employer, who as the result of a claim
-- src:2552 | made under this section has paid any salary to a workman, from
-- src:2553 | instituting civil proceedings for the recovery of the amount of salary
-- src:2554 | so paid from the employer of that workman.
@ref s 65(3) (src:2550-2554)
GIVEN `the person is a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, who as the result of a claim made under this section has paid salary to a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(3) this section prevents the person from instituting civil proceedings against the employer for the recovery of the salary paid` MEANS
    IF `the person is a principal, contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, who as the result of a claim made under this section has paid salary to a workman`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section prevents any principal or contractor or subcontractor, not being the employer, who as the result of a claim made under this section has paid any salary to a workman, from instituting civil proceedings for the recovery of the amount of salary so paid from the employer" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) speaks only of a person who has paid salary as the result of a claim under this section
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2556 | (4) Nothing in this section prevents a workman from recovering
-- src:2557 | salary under this Act from his or her employer instead of the principal
-- src:2558 | or contractor or subcontractor.
@ref s 65(4) (src:2556-2558)
GIVEN `the workman recovers salary under this Act from the employer instead of the principal or contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(4) this section prevents the workman from recovering salary from the employer instead` MEANS
    IF `the workman recovers salary under this Act from the employer instead of the principal or contractor or subcontractor`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section prevents a workman from recovering salary under this Act from his or her employer instead of the principal or contractor or subcontractor" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) speaks only of recovering salary from the employer instead of the principal, contractor or subcontractor
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2560 | (5) The reference to principal in this section includes a reference to
-- src:2561 | the Government or a statutory body or authority acting in the course
-- src:2562 | of or in the discharge of its functions.
@ref s 65(5) (src:2560-2562)
GIVEN `the person is the Government or a statutory body or authority acting in the course of or in the discharge of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(5) the person is a principal for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Government or a statutory body or authority acting in the course of or in the discharge of its functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The reference to principal in this section includes a reference to the Government or a statutory body or authority", which opens the class
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 66 Registration of contractors and subcontractors`

DECLARE `s 66(1) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(1) the person`

DECLARE `s 66(1) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(1) act as a contractor or a subcontractor without being registered`

-- src:2566 | 66.—(1) The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, require
-- src:2567 | all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the
-- src:2568 | Commissioner and thereafter a person must not act as a contractor
-- src:2569 | or a subcontractor unless the person is so registered.
@ref s 66(1) (src:2566-2569)
GIVEN `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(1) the person may act as a contractor or a subcontractor` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner` AND (NOT `the person is registered`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person must not act as a contractor or a subcontractor unless the person is so registered" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement begins only "thereafter", once the Minister has required registration by notification in the Gazette
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 66(1) (src:2566-2569)
GIVEN `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 66(1) Actor` `s 66(1) Action`
`s 66(1) the person's prohibition on acting as a contractor or subcontractor without registration` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner` AND (NOT `the person is registered`)
    THEN PARTY `s 66(1) the person`
         SHANT `s 66(1) act as a contractor or a subcontractor without being registered`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 66(1) the person` BECAUSE "the person acted as a contractor or a subcontractor without being registered with the Commissioner"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The prohibition of subsection (1) as a yes/no question of its own (ruled 2026-11-05, the
-- "thereafter" period and the "unless" bar): JUST FALSE before the Minister's notification
-- (the prohibition begins "thereafter"), JUST TRUE after it while the person is not registered,
-- JUST FALSE once the person is registered.  "May the person act" above is never answered yes
-- on the strength of the bar alone.
@ref s 66(1) (src:2566-2569)
GIVEN `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(1) the prohibition on acting as a contractor or a subcontractor without registration applies to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and thereafter a person must not act as a contractor or a subcontractor" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): before the Minister's notification the prohibition has not begun
        IF NOT `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, required all contractors and subcontractors to be registered with the Commissioner` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person is so registered" -- the person is registered, so the bar is lifted
        IF `the person is registered` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
-- src:2571 | (2) Every application for such registration must be in the prescribed
-- src:2572 | form.
@ref s 66(2) (src:2571-2572)
GIVEN `the application for registration is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(2) the application for registration is acceptable` MEANS
    IF `the application for registration is in the prescribed form`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says what an application must be, and does not say that one in the prescribed form is accepted
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every application for such registration must be in the prescribed form" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2574 | (3) Every person so registered under this section as a contractor or
-- src:2575 | subcontractor is deemed to be the employer of the workmen
-- src:2576 | employed by that person.
@ref s 66(3) (src:2574-2576)
GIVEN `the person is registered under this section as a contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(3) the person is deemed to be the employer of the workmen employed by that person` MEANS
    IF `the person is registered under this section as a contractor or subcontractor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person so registered under this section as a contractor or subcontractor"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2578 | (4) Every contractor or subcontractor who has been so registered
-- src:2579 | and who changes the name under which that contractor or
-- src:2580 | subcontractor carries on business must within 7 days of the change
-- src:2581 | of name apply in writing to the Commissioner for re‑registration and
-- src:2582 | cancellation of the previous registration.
@ref s 66(4) (src:2578-2582)
GIVEN `the day of the change of name` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 66(4) the last day for applying for re-registration` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the day of the change of name` 7 `the public holidays` FALSE

@ref s 66(4) (src:2578-2582)
GIVEN `the contractor or subcontractor is registered and changes the name under which the contractor or subcontractor carries on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the change of name` IS A DATE
      `the day the application in writing for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration was made to the Commissioner` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(4) the application for re-registration was made within 7 days of the change of name` MEANS
    IF `the contractor or subcontractor is registered and changes the name under which the contractor or subcontractor carries on business`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `s 66(4) the last day for applying for re-registration` `the day of the change of name` `the public holidays`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the count of days comes from the Interpretation Act module, which gives no answer
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the day the application in writing for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration was made to the Commissioner` AT MOST last)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every contractor or subcontractor who has been so registered and who changes the name"
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 66(4) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(4) the contractor or subcontractor`

DECLARE `s 66(4) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(4) apply in writing to the Commissioner for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration`

@ref s 66(4) (src:2578-2582)
GIVEN `the number of days from the change of name to the last day for applying` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 66(4) Actor` `s 66(4) Action`
`s 66(4) the contractor's or subcontractor's duty to apply for re-registration` MEANS
    PARTY `s 66(4) the contractor or subcontractor`
    MUST `s 66(4) apply in writing to the Commissioner for re-registration and cancellation of the previous registration`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the change of name to the last day for applying`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 66(4) the contractor or subcontractor` BECAUSE "the contractor or subcontractor did not apply in writing to the Commissioner for re-registration within 7 days of the change of name"

-- src:2584 | (5) The Commissioner may effect the registration of any person
-- src:2585 | under this section and may cancel any such registration.
@ref s 66(5) (src:2584-2585)
GIVEN `the person is the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(5) the Commissioner may effect the registration of a person and may cancel the registration` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Commissioner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commissioner may effect the registration of any person under this section and may cancel any such registration"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2591 | (7) Any person who contravenes this section shall be guilty of an
-- src:2592 | offence.
@ref s 66(7) (src:2591-2592)
